{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794213568,"nonce":"5snmqHByg8dLJVdQjHwsXP+D1BA=","title":"russl toy: a live shader playground built with Blinc","message":"A Blinc app for writing russl and seeing it draw, for people who think in pictures. A development tool, so it compiles at run time through russl_compiler; shipped apps still use build-time artifacts.\n\n- Editor: Blinc's code widget (search, IME), russl diagnostics shown inline at the offending token.\n- Preview: a full-screen quad through Blinc's custom render pass; recompiles on a short debounce after edits and keeps the last good pipeline while the source has errors.\n- Prelude: a `toy` library module with one uniform (time, resolution, mouse, frame), so a sketch starts at the fragment entry point.\n- Pipeline constants as controls: each #[pipeline] constant shows as a toggle or slider, and changing it re-specialises.\n- Output tabs: the WGSL, MSL, HLSL and GLSL russl produced.\n- Web: russl_compiler and naga build to wasm, so the same app can run in a browser through Blinc's web target.\n\nPlacement: in the russl repo, depending on Blinc by git, so Blinc's published crates take no russl dependency and the toy uses Blinc the way an outside app does. Name: \"russl toy\" or \"russl playground\", not Shadertoy.\n\nOrdering (owner, 2026-11-09): after the Blinc and russl integration work.","files":null}]}